Rāma sends Śatrughna away and rules happily --- Old brāhmaṇa brings dead boy to palace gate --- Brāhmaṇa wails son son with piteous words --- Brāhmaṇa recalls no lie or violence in his life --- Brāhmaṇa calls untimely death unseen in Rāma's realm --- Brāhmaṇa blames royal fault and demands revival --- Brāhmaṇa clasps son while censuring Rāma